  "notes": {
    "cnt_api": "**Booking API**\n\nThe only front door. Everything the app can do is a call to this service; nothing else in the platform is reachable from the internet.\n\n#squad: Sell",
    "mod_apportion": "**Revenue Apportionment**\n\nDoes not exist yet. Today RESERVA apportions revenue between operators as a side effect of holding the reservation, so this has to be built before the mainframe can be switched off.",
    "mod_barcode": "**Barcode Signing**\n\nSecurity-critical. Produces the signed payload a gateline scans offline. Key rotation is manual today and that is the single largest piece of operational risk in Fulfilment.\n\n#squad: Fulfil",
    "mod_gateline": "**Gateline Entitlements**\n\nBridge code, written to be deleted. Reads orders, writes an entitlement batch into RESERVA overnight, and reconciles the acknowledgement in the morning. Goes away in phase 3.",
    "mod_quote": "**Price Quote**\n\nTurns an itinerary into a price using the published fare tables plus any railcard the passenger holds. Pure function of its inputs - no state, no side effects, which is why it is the easiest module to test.",
    "mod_refunds": "**Refund Engine**\n\nAutomatic on declared disruption, manual otherwise. Sized for a normal day; a strike day is roughly twenty times the volume and the queue is the first thing to watch.\n\n#squad: Care",
    "mod_wallet": "**Wallet Delivery**\n\nPushes the signed ticket to the phone and emails a copy. The open question is whether it must validate fully offline; the answer changes the barcode format.",
    "sys_reserva": "**RESERVA**\n\n1994 reservation mainframe. Two write paths remain: the seat hold at checkout and the nightly gateline batch. Retirement is scheduled for June 2027 and blocked on apportionment finding an owner.\n\n#squad: Platform"
  },
